   [
    0.117,
    "The key fact: the square root of a product is the product of the square roots."
   ],
   [
    5.534,
    "For example, the square root of nine times four is the square root of thirty-six, which is six."
   ],
   [
    12.721,
    "And the square root of nine times the square root of four is three times two, also six."
   ],
   [
    19.154,
    "So we can split a radical into factors, and simplify the ones that are perfect squares."
   ]
  ]
