    "When the perfect square isn't obvious, use prime factors."
   ],
   [
    4.154,
    "Take the square root of seventy-two."
   ],
   [
    6.81,
    "Break seventy-two into primes: two, two, two, three, three."
   ],
   [
    12.266,
    "Under a square root, every pair of equal factors is a perfect square."
